{"title":"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an arithmetic sequence, the sum of the first and third terms is 6 and the sum of the second and fourth terms is 20. Determine the tenth term in the sequence.\n</p><p>(An arithmetic sequence is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8115da3f4f59130fedb4da4484dbf2fd5c83686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\text{, } 5\\text{, } 7\\text{, } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> are the first four terms of an arithmetic sequence.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th term of the sequence and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the common difference (the number that is added to get to the next time). The first four terms of the sequence are then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c7f7ddb681e3d199a370b84dc1efe7667a7280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1), f(1) + d, f(1) + 2d, f(1) + 3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the first term and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43fea34e0bbaa1906de4e3866aa0b7978c82d042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + f(1) + 2d = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6cae52026800b18d31f1cefa705a866e3530ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(1) + 2d = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c87407e9fb459c1952162fb8ebe664d925fd8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + d = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the second term and the fourth term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f457d680365e6ca1cfb25cc5f55d24144d3c6dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + d + f(1) + 3d = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5555aa7830b291c9cc217c4c3ab62df128dc5864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(1) + 4d = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6cae52026800b18d31f1cefa705a866e3530ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(1) + 2d = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5555aa7830b291c9cc217c4c3ab62df128dc5864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(1) + 4d = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703a05dac181b31397b51f92b4f060abae502a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(1) + 4d - 2f(1) - 2d = 20 - 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edabfdc67726e7b8f402c636135f8427aec6ac68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2d = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cbe332f498f14c2441bc4a7c5c26fcbb71cb167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{14}{2} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Plugging this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131f1214c099fc7bfb4c649316d97168c300ee95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + d = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e07735ddd784787de38ee288bd35ea8186df72e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + 7 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/82564bf549e139322d79b761b52374c097016b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 3 - 7 = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every time we go from one term to the next, so we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/940ecf6711969c95460f0d5a7e47489c7a131c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c28a474b6f750a00b497bb4346c625b8a1f0472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(10) = f(1) + 9d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43bec8526048fd3fd20bf93b04137c80ffc47ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(10) = -4 + 9 \\times 7 = -4 + 63 = \\boxed{59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"297\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.119 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4989/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.241      1 2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    6.241      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36038:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232359 and revision id 279718. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}